--TEST--
`$this` in a `static` method is refused rather than read, and the same body's own class name is still reachable — `rule:statements/static-is-a-member-modifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A static method is entered with no receiver, so the checker declares no
// `$this` in one (`crate::check`) and a read of it is E0779 rather than the
// undeclared-name diagnostic: there is no declaration a program could add.
class Config {
    private int $size = 1;

    // Declared `mixed` so that the recovery type `check_read` answers with
    // satisfies it: the case pins the refusal, not the return-type mismatch a
    // narrower declaration would cascade into.
    public static function limit(): mixed {
        return $this->size;
    }
}

Config::limit();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0779]: `$this` names the receiver of an instance method, and this body has none
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
